21/09/2026 11:58:13 PM | INFO     | step_1.py:<module>:133 - content=[{'type': 'text', 'text': 'According to the report, projecting oil demand displacement from EV adoption requires the integration of three analytical layers:\n\n*   The annual sales trajectory for new EVs.\n*   The retirement rate of the existing internal combustion engine (ICE) fleet.\n*   The average annual mileage and fuel economy of the vehicles being displaced.\n\nThe report notes that because there are approximately 1.4 billion passenger vehicles globally—the vast majority being ICE vehicles—and because vehicle lifetimes typically range from 15 to 20 years (or longer in developing markets), complete fleet electrification cannot occur in less than two decades.\n\nRegarding the impact of these trajectories, the report finds:\n*   **Near term (through 2030):** EV penetration will shave "meaningful but modest" volumes from global oil demand growth, likely delaying demand peaks rather than preventing them and offering only partial insulation against supply-driven price shocks.\n*   **Long term (2030–2050):** Cumulative fleet electrification could reduce oil demand by 20 to 30 million barrels per day, which is considered large enough to fundamentally restructure the oil supply curve and materially compress it.', 'extras': {'signature': 'EnEKbwFpFH0TSQsGVfGku00dJyd7YSODm1gpYSoFjy0Ejcs/Ov1AXSKp/nG0UPCU7BlWYyG80+Mh4mzS3w+OAI1HJLzyvXn9OwuQkjk1VnyTa4ZPR8iYnZBU+2nfA/MbgNPQDiNv6of3qN/ulTAXMD4/Lw=='}}] additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'finish_reason': 'STOP', 'model_name': 'gemini-3.1-flash-lite', 'safety_ratings': [], 'model_provider': 'google_genai'} id='lc_run--01a0c539-ab3a-7c32-97e6-7e6ceb0c598f-0' tool_calls=[] invalid_tool_calls=[] usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 891, 'output_tokens': 241, 'total_tokens': 1132, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 0}}
